abel><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">14.6%</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Visits that added something</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 7 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:55%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">26</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 10 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">47</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Organic visits that saw the page</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 7 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:97%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">300</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 10 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">310</span></div></div></div><p class=\"note\">Up 70% on /std-test-pricing/, which clears the 9% that 10 days of traffic can actually resolve. Worth repeating elsewhere. 11 days are left out of this because the site recorded no carts on them.</p></div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>Place My Order double-click fix</b><span class=\"flag funnel\">funnel</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 21 &middot; 8:30 AM</span></div><p class=\"note\">The button stayed live after the first click, so a second click created another Stripe invoice for the same order. Five of the first 19 paid orders went through two or three invoices.</p><div class=\"vh\"><span class=\"vb flat\">No change detected</span><span class=\"vd\">measured on checkout</span></div><div class=\"cmp\"><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Orders needing a second attempt</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0%</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 27 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0%</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Orders that retried</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 27 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Paid orders a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 27 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">4</span></div></div></div><p class=\"note\">Reads +0% on checkout, inside the 100% that 27 days can resolve, so this is noise rather than a result. It has not made anything worse either.</p></div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>Checkout stops re-asking for a lab</b><span class=\"flag funnel\">funnel</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 21 &middot; 8:50 AM</span></div><p class=\"note\">Checkout showed the whole Test Centers module again even when the shopper had already picked a location, worst on mobile. It now shows the chosen lab with a single Change Location button.</p><div class=\"vh\"><span class=\"vb flat\">No change detected</span><span class=\"vd\">measured on checkout</span></div><div class=\"cmp\"><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Paid orders per 100 carts</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0.0%</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 16 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">4.6%</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Paid orders a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 16 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">6</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Carts a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:79%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">87</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 16 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">110</span></div></div></div><p class=\"note\">Reads +0% on checkout, inside the 20% that 16 days can resolve, so this is noise rather than a result. It has not made anything worse either. 11 days are left out of this because the site recorded no carts on them.</p></div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>GEO button to pricing page</b><span class=\"flag funnel\">funnel</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 19 &middot; morning</span></div><p class=\"note\">Clicking Choose This Location on an STD city page now goes to the STD pricing page instead of the city list. Raised and fixed the same day.</p><div class=\"vh\"><span class=\"vb good\">Looks better</span><span class=\"vd\">measured on /std-testing/</span></div><div class=\"cmp\"><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Carts per 1,000 organic visits</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 1 day</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:42%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">35.2</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 18 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">84.6</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Carts a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 1 day</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:54%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">23</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 18 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">42</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Organic visits a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 1 day</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">653</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 18 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:76%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">496</span></div></div></div><p class=\"note\">Up 140% on /std-testing/, which clears the 7% that 18 days of traffic can actually resolve. Visits moved -24%, but 496 is normal for those weekdays (usual 451), so traffic is not the story. Worth repeating elsewhere. 11 days are left out of this because the site recorded no carts on them.</p></div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>Monetization live</b><span class=\"flag launch\">launch</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 18 &middot; 12:00 AM</span></div><p class=\"note\">Checkout opened on testing.com. First customer order came through at 1:03 AM from Google organic.</p><p class=\"note\">This is the starting line, so there is nothing before it to compare against.</p></div><h3 class=\"mini\">Cart rate since launch</h3><div class=\"chartwrap\"><canvas id=\"chg_chart\"></canvas></div><p class=\"note\">Carts per 1,000 organic visits, split by the section each change affected, with the whole site dashed for reference. Only changes measured on cart rate appear here. Checkout changes move a different number and are judged on their own cards above, and a change to a page people click through to rather than land on gets its own chart below. A section line is the only place a section-level change can show up: STD GEO is about a tenth of our visits, so a big move there barely dents the sitewide line. Carts are the measure rather than orders because orders run single digits a day and cannot separate signal from noise for weeks. 31 days of data so far.</p><h3 class=\"mini\">Cart rate on /std-test-pricing/</h3><div class=\"chartwrap\"><canvas id=\"chg_page_chart\"></canvas></div><p class=\"note\">Share of organic visits to /std-test-pricing/ that add something to the cart. Counted on the page people <b>viewed</b>, not the page they landed on, which is why this is a separate chart and not another line above. Almost nobody arrives on the pricing page from search, they click through to it, so its landing-page numbers run single digits a day while it fires more than half of every cart on the site. One visit counts once here however many tests it adds, so this is a share of people rather than a count of clicks. The two charts count different groups of people and their heights do not compare.</p><p class=\"note\">Changes are recorded by hand, big ones only, and each needs the right <code>scope</code> and <code>metric</code>. To add one, edit <code>changes.json</code>.</p></section>","impact":{"labels":["Aug 18","Aug 19","Aug 20","Aug 21","Aug 22","Aug 23","Aug 24","Aug 25","Aug 26","Aug 27","Aug 28","Aug 29","Aug 30","Aug 31","Sep 1","Sep 2","Sep 3","Sep 4","Sep 5","Sep 6","Sep 7","Sep 8","Sep 9","Sep 10","Sep 11","Sep 12","Sep 13","Sep 14","Sep 15","Sep 16","Sep 17"],"dates":["2026-08-18","2026-08-19","2026-08-20","2026-08-21","2026-08-22","2026-08-23","2026-08-24","2026-08-25","2026-08-26","2026-08-27","2026-08-28","2026-08-29","2026-08-30","2026-08-31","2026-09-01","2026-09-02","2026-09-03","2026-09-04","2026-09-05","2026-09-06","2026-09-07","2026-09-08","2026-09-09","2026-09-10","2026-09-11","2026-09-12","2026-09-13","2026-09-14","2026-09-15","2026-09-16","2026-09-17"],"series":[{"label":"Whole site cart rate","scope":"sitewide","rate":[14.9,15.7,15.4,16.5,15.1,13.1,15.4,13.3,22.3,5.2,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,0.0,null,7.4,13.1,19.6,23.6,22.9,24.8,21.8,20.9,22.6,22.